<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss money market steady, SNB adds at 1-5/8 pct.</title>
<headline>Swiss money market steady, SNB adds at 1-5/8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Swiss money market was stable with short-term rates steady, dealers said.</p>
<p>Tomorrow/next money was quoted around 1.50 to 1.75 percent in the market and the Swiss National Bank (SNB) also added short-term funds to the market at 1-5/8 percent, similar to Friday's injection.</p>
<p>Dealers see the market remaining stable with rates around the current level for the time being.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
